    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness-tools/ns/glossary/kg-schema-fields/graph-typology-registry.graphtypologydef.layer",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness-tools/ns/glossary/kg-schema-fields"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "GraphTypologyDef.layer",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Whose namespace the kind is named in, when it is not the harness's: `core` for a kind the content layer above the harness declares as a node in its own `typologies/` graph, named in THAT layer's namespace ({@link graphTypologyIri}, {@link DECLARED_BY}). The harness registers no `core` kind in code since folio-assistant#2598 (owner, 2026-10-16, \"1a\"): the ones it uses itself (`todos`, `library`, `uploads`, `voices`, `folio`, …) are its own. A kind bootstrap defines is bootstrap's whatever this says (`BOOTSTRAP_GRAPH_TYPOLOGIES`). The kind IS its individual, `<ns>graphTypology/<name>` ({@link graphTypologyIri}); there is no class per kind. Owner, 2026-09-30 (bean `3r47`): \"Drop per-kind classes\" — bootstrap names a kind as one `GraphTypology` individual, and the harness now does the same.",
          "@language": "en"
        }
      ],
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness-tools/schemas/kg/graph-typology-registry.ts#GraphTypologyDef.layer",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
